---
import { Image } from 'astro:assets';
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import SiteHeader from '../components/SiteHeader.astro';
import portraitImage from '../assets/images/hassan-portrait.png';
---

<Layout
	title="About Hassan Mujtaba | Product Designer & UX Architect"
	description="About Hassan Mujtaba, a Product Designer & UX Architect focused on AI-enabled, data-driven SaaS platforms and complex enterprise systems."
>
	<a class="skip-link" href="#main-content">Skip to content</a>

	<div class="page">
		<SiteHeader />

		<main id="main-content">
			<section class="hero">
				<p class="eyebrow">About</p>
				<div class="hero-layout">
					<div class="hero-copy">
						<h1 class="display-title">I design complex systems by aligning user goals, business strategy, and system logic.</h1>
						<p class="hero-text">
							I'm Hassan, a Product Designer & UX Architect with 12+ years of experience
							designing AI-enabled, data-driven SaaS platforms and complex enterprise systems —
							turning dense workflows and multi-module products into experiences people can
							navigate with confidence.
						</p>
					</div>
					<div class="hero-portrait-wrap">
						<Image
							class="hero-portrait"
							src={portraitImage}
							alt="Portrait of Muhammad Hassan Mujtaba"
							loading="eager"
							decoding="async"
							widths={[320, 480, 640]}
							sizes="(max-width: 980px) 100vw, 32vw"
						/>
					</div>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">Background</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						Over 12+ years I've worked across enterprise intelligence, solar/renewable energy
						ERP, and healthcare platforms — domains where the design challenge is rarely just
						about making something look good. More often, it's about structuring multi-module
						SaaS systems that scale with operational complexity while staying usable under
						real-world pressure.
					</p>
					<p>
						I partner with product and engineering teams to translate complexity into
						structured, scalable solutions — across AI-integrated systems, enterprise SaaS
						products, intelligence platforms, healthcare systems, and renewable energy.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">How I Work</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						My process runs Understand → Research → Architect → Design → Validate → Deliver,
						with AI woven through every stage rather than bolted on at the end — from
						AI-assisted discovery and layout exploration to AI-supported usability analysis
						and AI-generated documentation for faster developer handoff.
					</p>
					<p>
						I believe every complex system can be structured: product experience sits at the
						intersection of user goals, business goals, and system logic, and my job is finding
						where those three actually overlap.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>

			<section class="editorial-section">
				<div class="section-rail">
					<p class="section-kicker">Focus</p>
				</div>
				<div class="story-block">
					<p>
						AI-integrated product systems, business-aligned architecture, and cross-functional
						product influence — designing intelligent workflows that enhance enterprise
						decision-making, structuring multi-module SaaS systems that scale, and translating
						constraints into structured interaction models alongside product and engineering.
					</p>
					<p>
						I'm especially interested in data-dense dashboards, workflow tools, and AI-assisted
						interfaces where reducing friction has a measurable impact on how confident people
						feel using the system.
					</p>
				</div>
			</section>
		</main>
	</div>
</Layout>

<style>
	.page {
		position: relative;
		width: min(calc(100% - 3rem), 78rem);
		margin: 0 auto;
		padding: 1.25rem 0 5rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-kicker {
		font-family: var(--font-mono);
		font-size: 0.82rem;
		font-weight: 600;
		letter-spacing: 0.08em;
		line-height: 1.4;
		text-transform: uppercase;
	}

	.hero {
		padding: 6rem 0 4rem;
	}

	.hero-layout {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1.35fr) minmax(15rem, 20rem);
		gap: 2.5rem;
		align-items: start;
		margin-top: 1rem;
	}

	.hero-copy {
		max-width: 52rem;
	}

	.eyebrow,
	.section-kicker {
		margin: 0;
		color: var(--muted-foreground);
		font-style: normal;
	}

	.hero-text,
	.story-block p {
		font-size: 1.08rem;
		line-height: 1.7;
		margin: 0;
	}

	.hero-text {
		max-width: 44rem;
		margin-top: 1.5rem;
	}

	.hero-portrait-wrap {
		display: flex;
		justify-content: flex-end;
		align-self: start;
		padding-top: 0.35rem;
	}

	.hero-portrait {
		width: min(100%, 20rem);
		height: auto;
		display: block;
		border-radius: 1.5rem;
		box-shadow: 0 18px 40px rgba(23, 23, 23, 0.08);
	}

	.editorial-section {
		display: grid;
		grid-template-columns: 16rem minmax(0, 1fr);
		gap: 2rem;
		padding: 2.5rem 0;
		border-top: 1px solid var(--border);
	}

	.section-rail {
		align-self: start;
	}

	.story-block {
		display: grid;
		gap: 1rem;
		max-width: 52rem;
	}

	@media (max-width: 1100px) {
		.hero-layout {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
			gap: 1.75rem;
			align-items: start;
		}

		.hero-copy {
			max-width: 100%;
		}

		.hero-text {
			max-width: 42rem;
		}

		.hero-portrait-wrap {
			justify-content: flex-start;
			padding-top: 0;
		}
	}

	@media (max-width: 720px) {
		.page {
			width: min(calc(100% - 1.5rem), 78rem);
			padding-top: 1rem;
		}

		.hero {
			padding: 4rem 0 3rem;
		}

		.editorial-section {
			grid-template-columns: 1fr;
		}

		.hero-text,
		.story-block p {
			font-size: 1.05rem;
		}

		.hero-portrait {
			width: min(100%, 16rem);
		}
	}
</style>
